{"id":"ux-usability-testing","title":"UI/UX: usability testing","subject":"UI/UX design","label":"UI/UX design","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":164,"duration":164.48,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":472,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"The puzzle","start":0,"end":15.715},{"id":"explain","title":"What it is","start":15.715,"end":54.375},{"id":"explain2","title":"Small rounds","start":54.375,"end":83.585},{"id":"example","title":"Search example","start":83.585,"end":104.275},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":104.275,"end":111.965},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":111.965,"end":120.655},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":120.655,"end":141.975},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":141.975,"end":164.48}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":5.16,"text":"Have you ever watched someone use something you designed and felt surprised by where they got stuck?","w":[0.52,0.68,0.9,1.14,1.54,1.96,2.14,2.48,2.64,3.2,3.34,3.58,4.12,4.36,4.52,4.66,4.86]},{"s":0,"a":5.61,"b":11.39,"text":"I'm Kora. Today we look at usability testing, a simple way to see your design through real eyes.","w":[5.72,5.9,6.76,7.14,7.28,7.46,7.64,8.18,8.96,9.08,9.4,9.62,9.76,9.92,10.1,10.48,10.74,11.1]},{"s":0,"a":11.69,"b":15.29,"text":"It is one of the simplest ways to improve a design before you build it.","w":[11.74,11.86,12.04,12.16,12.26,12.44,12.9,13.22,13.4,13.9,13.98,14.5,14.8,14.92,15.18]},{"s":1,"a":16.14,"b":20.85,"text":"Usability testing means watching real people try to do real tasks with your design.","w":[16.24,16.84,17.26,17.6,18.04,18.32,18.74,18.98,19.1,19.3,19.64,20.14,20.28,20.46]},{"s":1,"a":21.15,"b":26.22,"text":"It checks whether the design works for them. You are testing the design, never the person.","w":[21.2,21.34,21.68,21.96,22.08,22.5,22.78,22.92,23.64,23.8,23.96,24.4,24.52,25.42,25.66,25.78]},{"s":1,"a":26.52,"b":30.88,"text":"You watch what they do, not what they say they like. It is about behaviour.","w":[26.54,26.7,27,27.18,27.36,28.08,28.28,28.46,28.66,28.86,29.04,29.86,29.96,30.08,30.36]},{"s":1,"a":31.18,"b":37,"text":"Pick three to five people who are like your real users. Write realistic tasks as goals, not instructions.","w":[31.2,31.42,31.66,31.78,32.04,32.32,32.46,32.58,32.76,32.92,33.26,33.98,34.24,34.78,35.2,35.36,36.1,36.3]},{"s":1,"a":37.3,"b":42.16,"text":"Say, you want to send two thousand to your sister. Do not say, tap the send button.","w":[37.38,37.74,37.88,38.04,38.16,38.44,38.68,39.12,39.22,39.42,40.2,40.36,40.56,41.2,41.46,41.58,41.82]},{"s":1,"a":42.46,"b":47.11,"text":"Ask them to think aloud as they work. Then stay quiet. Do not help or explain.","w":[42.54,42.76,42.94,43.08,43.3,43.68,43.78,43.94,44.64,44.88,45.16,45.94,46.08,46.26,46.48,46.6]},{"s":1,"a":47.41,"b":53.95,"text":"If they are stuck, ask, what would you expect to happen? Note where they hesitate, go wrong, or give up.","w":[47.48,47.58,47.74,47.92,48.46,49.18,49.34,49.5,49.64,49.96,50.08,51,51.22,51.38,51.54,52.4,52.62,53.3,53.44,53.72]},{"s":2,"a":54.8,"b":60.22,"text":"Afterwards, group the problems. Fix the most serious ones first, then test again.","w":[54.88,55.82,56.06,56.18,57.24,57.5,57.6,57.86,58.34,58.56,59.3,59.54,59.84]},{"s":2,"a":60.52,"b":67.54,"text":"Jakob Nielsen's research found that testing with about five users uncovers most usability problems, roughly eighty five percent.","w":[60.62,61.02,61.54,62.06,62.32,62.5,62.92,63.08,63.4,63.8,64.24,64.8,65.1,65.62,66.38,66.74,66.96,67.2]},{"s":2,"a":67.84,"b":74.4,"text":"So several small rounds beat one big one. You can test a paper sketch or a clickable prototype long before any code.","w":[67.9,68.14,68.58,68.9,69.28,69.64,69.8,70.08,70.64,70.76,70.94,71.24,71.32,71.62,72.12,72.22,72.28,72.7,73.3,73.56,73.9,74.08]},{"s":2,"a":74.7,"b":80.13,"text":"You can also measure whether they completed the task, how long it took, and how many errors they made.","w":[74.74,74.88,75.06,75.36,75.86,76.12,76.26,76.7,76.8,77.54,77.74,77.98,78.08,78.78,78.94,79.12,79.4,79.68,79.84]},{"s":2,"a":80.43,"b":83.16,"text":"This is why small tests are practical and affordable.","w":[80.5,80.74,80.84,81.08,81.38,81.76,81.92,82.54,82.66]},{"s":3,"a":84.01,"b":86.09,"text":"Imagine five testers try your app.","w":[84.06,84.58,84.88,85.4,85.64,85.88]},{"s":3,"a":86.39,"b":90.58,"text":"Three of them cannot find the search because it hides behind an icon with no label.","w":[86.42,86.72,86.82,87.02,87.38,87.64,87.78,88.3,88.54,88.66,89.02,89.36,89.52,89.86,90.06,90.24]},{"s":3,"a":90.88,"b":95.35,"text":"The fix is a visible search field with the word Search. Then you test again.","w":[90.92,91.1,91.52,91.64,91.74,92.16,92.44,92.82,93,93.1,93.48,94.4,94.62,94.76,95.04]},{"s":3,"a":95.65,"b":99.48,"text":"You learned that from watching behaviour, not from asking for opinions.","w":[95.66,95.86,96.12,96.28,96.48,96.86,97.86,98.08,98.36,98.7,98.88]},{"s":3,"a":99.78,"b":103.85,"text":"In the next round, if testers find the search straight away, your fix worked.","w":[99.84,99.92,100.06,100.32,100.82,100.96,101.44,101.7,101.84,102.16,102.42,103,103.22,103.46]},{"s":4,"a":104.7,"b":109.01,"text":"During a test, the person asks you, where do I tap? What should you do?","w":[104.72,105,105.08,105.5,105.64,106.1,106.36,106.88,107.1,107.26,107.38,108.26,108.44,108.64,108.78]},{"s":4,"a":109.46,"b":111.54,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[109.48,109.8,110.06,110.18,110.48,111,111.2]},{"s":5,"a":112.39,"b":120.23,"text":"Do not show them. Ask what they would try or expect, and note the problem. That keeps the test about the design, not their performance.","w":[112.42,112.6,112.86,113.08,113.82,114.04,114.16,114.28,114.48,114.82,114.96,115.8,115.98,116.18,116.3,117.08,117.26,117.54,117.66,117.94,118.16,118.28,119.2,119.42,119.6]},{"s":6,"a":121.08,"b":125.95,"text":"Testing only with teammates or friends is a mistake. Choose people like your real users.","w":[121.1,121.58,121.8,121.98,122.46,122.6,122.96,123.08,123.14,124.18,124.5,124.82,125,125.16,125.48]},{"s":6,"a":126.25,"b":130.87,"text":"Giving hints or defending the design is another. Stay quiet and watch behaviour.","w":[126.3,126.62,127.04,127.18,127.62,127.74,128.2,128.34,129.24,129.52,129.96,130.1,130.36]},{"s":6,"a":131.17,"b":139.78,"text":"Asking do you like it, or testing once at the very end, is also weak. Ask what they expected, and test early, fix, then test again.","w":[131.26,131.62,131.7,131.84,132.1,132.62,132.78,133.24,133.44,133.52,133.64,133.96,134.6,134.74,135.04,136.04,136.28,136.4,136.56,137.42,137.54,137.86,138.46,139.06,139.24,139.5]},{"s":6,"a":140.08,"b":141.55,"text":"Keep the focus on behaviour.","w":[140.12,140.38,140.5,140.96,141.06]},{"s":7,"a":142.4,"b":148.14,"text":"Usability testing watches real people do real tasks, and you test the design, not the person.","w":[142.5,143.04,143.5,143.94,144.2,144.56,144.82,145.12,145.98,146.1,146.24,146.52,146.64,147.46,147.66,147.76]},{"s":7,"a":148.44,"b":152.32,"text":"Use three to five users, realistic goals, and quiet observation.","w":[148.58,148.82,149.1,149.22,149.58,150.02,150.54,150.98,151.18,151.66]},{"s":7,"a":152.62,"b":156.57,"text":"Group problems, fix the worst first, and test again.","w":[152.64,152.98,154.04,154.34,154.48,154.84,155.68,155.84,156.2]},{"s":7,"a":156.87,"b":160.41,"text":"Top tip: several small tests beat one big test near the end.","w":[156.92,157.24,157.8,158.16,158.44,158.82,159.14,159.32,159.54,159.84,160,160.16]},{"s":7,"a":160.71,"b":163.88,"text":"Knowzone is here to help you keep practising with confidence.","w":[160.82,161.4,161.52,161.82,161.96,162.18,162.34,162.6,163.12,163.32]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"The puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Surprised where users get stuck?"},{"at":5.51,"kind":"term","text":"Usability testing","detail":"See your design through real eyes"},{"at":11.59,"kind":"text","text":"Improve design before you build"}]},{"at":15.89,"heading":"What it is","items":[{"at":16.04,"kind":"term","text":"Usability testing","detail":"Watching real people try real tasks with your design"},{"at":21.05,"kind":"text","text":"Test the design, never the person"},{"at":26.42,"kind":"text","text":"Watch behaviour, not opinions"},{"at":31.08,"kind":"text","text":"3–5 people like your real users"}]},{"at":37.05,"heading":"Tasks and think-aloud","items":[{"at":37.2,"kind":"text","text":"Goal: send 2,000 to your sister"},{"at":42.36,"kind":"text","text":"Ask them to think aloud; then stay quiet"},{"at":47.31,"kind":"text","text":"If stuck: ask what they expect; note problems"}]},{"at":54.55,"heading":"Small rounds","items":[{"at":54.7,"kind":"text","text":"Group problems; fix worst first; retest"},{"at":60.42,"kind":"term","text":"5 users ≈ 85% of problems","detail":"Nielsen: about five users uncover most usability problems"},{"at":67.74,"kind":"text","text":"Several small rounds beat one big one"},{"at":74.6,"kind":"text","text":"Measure completion, time, errors"},{"at":80.33,"kind":"text","text":"Small tests are practical and affordable"}]},{"at":83.76,"heading":"Search example","items":[{"at":83.91,"kind":"text","text":"Five testers try your app"},{"at":86.29,"kind":"text","text":"3/5 cannot find search: unlabelled icon"},{"at":90.78,"kind":"text","text":"Fix: visible search field labelled Search"},{"at":95.55,"kind":"text","text":"Learn from behaviour, not opinions"},{"at":99.68,"kind":"text","text":"Retest: search found straight away = fix worked"}]},{"at":104.28,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":104.28,"kind":"question","text":"During a test, the person asks you, where do I tap? What should you do?"}]},{"at":112.14,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":112.29,"kind":"text","text":"Don't show them"},{"at":112.29,"kind":"text","text":"Ask what they'd try or expect; note problem"},{"at":112.29,"kind":"text","text":"Keep test about design, not performance"}]},{"at":120.83,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":120.98,"kind":"wrong","text":"Testing only with teammates or friends"},{"at":126.15,"kind":"wrong","text":"Giving hints or defending the design"},{"at":131.07,"kind":"wrong","text":"Asking 'Do you like it?'; testing only at the end"},{"at":139.98,"kind":"text","text":"Keep the focus on behaviour"}]},{"at":142.15,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":142.3,"kind":"text","text":"Watch real people do real tasks"},{"at":148.34,"kind":"text","text":"3–5 users, realistic goals, quiet observation"},{"at":152.52,"kind":"text","text":"Group problems; fix worst; retest"},{"at":156.77,"kind":"tip","text":"Several small tests beat one big test near the end"},{"at":160.61,"kind":"text","text":"Knowzone: keep practising with confidence"}]}],"check":{"at":111.79,"seconds":10,"question":"During a test, the person asks you, where do I tap? What should you do?","answer":"Don't show them. Ask what they'd try or expect, and note the problem. Keep it about the design, not their performance."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}